QuestGuidance.Register("en",383,{
[12225]="70070B00\n1\tDefeat Badharál the Gorger\030Defeat Maukhorn\030Defeat the Legion of Lhaereth\030Defeat Zamâktar the Putrescent\tDefeat the threats that lurk within The Folly of Nagakhêdi.\n",
[12226]="70070B06\n1\tDefeat Badharál the Gorger\030Defeat Maukhorn\030Defeat the Legion of Lhaereth\030Defeat Zamâktar the Putrescent\tDefeat the threats that lurk within The Folly of Nagakhêdi.\n",
[12227]="7006658B\n1\tCollect worker's tools (total: 6)\tGonodil has asked you to collect all the worker's tools that have been left abandoned.\n2\tTalk to Gonodil in Barad Rill\tYou should tell Gonodil that you have collected all the tools. Gonodil can be found in Barad Rill.\n",
[12228]="70019D29\n1\tDeliver the sealed letter to Andiriniel at the Lady's Rest\tAndiriniel is at the Lady's Rest, south-west of the gates of Caras Galadhon. Hadhelen asked you to deliver his letter to Andiriniel.\n",
[12229]="70032BBC\n1\tCollect Orc-arrows\tOrc-arrows can be found near the East Arch of the Twenty-first Hall. You should collect Orc-arrows to show to the dwarves of the Twenty-first Hall.\n2\tCollect Orc-arrows (total: 6)\tOrc-arrows can be found near the East Arch of the Twenty-first Hall. You should collect Orc-arrows to show to the dwarves of the Twenty-first Hall.\n3\tBring the Orc-arrows to Foreman Mögr\tYou have stowed away many Orc-arrows to show to Mögr in the Twenty-first Hall. You should return to Mögr with the arrows you collected.\n",
[12230]="70046C4E\n1\tListen to Anborn's tale\tAnborn can be found at Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien. Anborn has offered to tell you more of the Halflings that passed through Ithilien.\n2\tTalk to Anborn in Henneth Annûn\tAnborn can be found at Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien. You have listened to Anborn's tale and should now ask if he knows more of the Halflings.\n",
[12231]="7001B0AE\n1\tTalk to Elrohir at the Ford of Bruinen\tElrohir and Elladan, sons of Elrond, are prepared to stand against the army of the Enemy attempting to cross the Bruinen. Elrohir is awaiting your arrival.\n2\tPush back the first assault\tThe first assault has been launched. The Ford and the sons of Elrond must be defended.\n3\tPush back the second assault\tThe second assault has been launched. The Enemy shows no signs of slowing.\n4\tPush back the third assault\tThe third assault has been launched. The Enemy appears to be wavering in morale and decreasing in number.\n5\tPush back the fourth assault\tThe fourth assault has been launched. The Enemy's forces are dwindling quickly and are nearly at their end.\n6\tFend off the final assault\tThe final assault begins as the leader of the Enemy's forces enters the battle. Defeat him, and the invasion will be thwarted\n",
[12232]="7002F104\n1\tDefeat Easterlings at the Ford (total: 10)\tThe Easterlings can be found at the Ford. Wulfin has asked you to venture to the Ford and defeat the Easterlings encamped there.\n2\tTalk to Wulfin\tWulfin can be found in Harwick. Wulfin will be pleased to hear you disrupted the Easterling-camp at the Ford.\n",
[12233]="7003031E\n1\tDestroy Cargûl-runes at the Ford (total: 6)\tRunes can be found on the paths the Cargûl of the Ford walk. Wulfin asked you to destroy the runes the Cargûl drop before they defile the land.\n2\tTalk to Wulfin\tWulfin is in Harwick. Wulfin will be pleased to hear that you destroyed several runes before they were able to defile the land.\n",
[12234]="7005C8D0\n1\tTalk to Sadorwen\tSadorwen is located in Bazanmanar. Golodhril has asked you to speak to her sister Sadorwen on her behalf.\n2\tReturn to Golodhril\tGolodhril is sulking in Bazanmanar. Sadorwen has suggested that you help Golodhril.\n",
[12235]="700303CF\n1\tStamp out Orc-fires (total: 8)\tOrc-fires can be found around the Orc-encampment near Wisewood. You should stamp out any Orc-fires you can find.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have snuffed out several Orc-fires on Wisewood's behalf, saving what is left of his ravaged grove.\n",
[12236]="7004CE25\n1\tHelp Sterkist gather his supplies\tMany of the Beornings' supplies were lost in the woods. You should help Sterkist gather his supplies by completing \"Scattered in the Forest.\"\n2\tTalk to Langhár\030Talk to Sterkist\tLanghár and Sterkist have gone to The Forest Gate, at the western end of Eryn Lasgalen. You should talk to Langhár and Sterkist.\n3\tTalk to Thranduil\tThe Beornings are safely on their way, and the Taurogrim have been exposed. You should report these events to King Thranduil.\n",
[12237]="70072F8A\n1\tDefeat Huorns east of Sul Madásh (total: 6)\tMálacál has asked that you travel to the east of Sul Madásh and help her and her hunters thin the number of blighted Huorns that can be found.\n2\tReturn to Málacál\tReturn to Málacál near Sul Madásh and report your success of defeating Huorns in eastern Adagím.\n",
[12238]="70028B64\n1\tInvestigate the Forges of Isengard\tBron is in Galtrev. You should speak with Bron to travel to the Forges of Isengard.\n2\tReturn to Bron in Galtrev\tBron is in Galtrev. You should speak with Bron to tell her of your success against Saruman's attempts to forge legendary weapons.\n",
[12239]="700076D0\n1\tSearch the ruins for Oddvarr's pack\tOddvarr asked you to search the ruins to the north. Oddvarr set his pack down somewhere in the area and cannot seem to remember where.\n2\tRetrieve Oddvarr's pack\tOddvarr awaits you to the south of the ruins. You found Oddvarr's pack in the old ruins to the north.\n3\tReturn Oddvarr's provisions\tOddvarr is by the haystacks south of the ruins where you found the pack. You found Oddvarr's pack containing his much-needed provisions.\n",
[12240]="7004544E\n1\tInvestigate Nardol Quarry\tNardol Quarry is located in south-western Taur Drúadan. You should investigate Nardol Quarry.\n2\tDefeat foes at Nardol Quarry (total: 10)\030Find the area where the Dheghûn are coming from\tEnemies and the source of these Dheghûn can be found at Nardol Quarry. You should defeat foes and explore Nardol Quarry.\n3\tSpeak with Rhûd-pulo-Drât at Nardol Quarry\tRhûd-pulo-Drât can be found in Nardol Quarry. You should speak with Rhûd-pulo-Drât.\n",
[12241]="7003046F\n1\tCollect food for the prisoner in the Snowbourn prison\tFastred wants you to bring a plate of food to a prisoner of Snowbourn. The food can be found in the prison, near the prisoner's cell.\n2\tDeliver the food to the prisoner\tThe prisoner can be found in the prison-house just outside the mead-hall in Snowbourn.\n3\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred can be found in the mead-hall of Snowbourn.\n",
[12242]="700173B7\n1\tTalk to Garthar in the Deep Descent\tGarthar is in the Deep Descent of Moria. Falgir confided in you about the discovery of crystals thought long lost, now turning up all throughout Moria. He has asked you to speak with Garthar to see if he can shed some light on the matter.\n2\tTalk to Falgir at the Deep Descent\tFalgir is in the Deep Descent in Moria. Garthar told you a bit of history of the vaults in Moria, what they held and how he fears that one such vault is breached. He now wishes you to tell Falgir what you have learned.\n",
[12243]="700173B6\n1\tBring the items to Falgir in the Deep Descent\030Collect swatches of fabric (total: 12)\tThe Forgotten Treasury lies to the south and south-east of the Deep Descent. Falgir has asked that you kill Orcs and goblins between the Deep Descent and Forgotten Treasury to ready yourself for the task of liberating the vault. He also asked you to collect scraps of material from the Orcs and goblins.\n",
[12244]="700544A3\n1\tDefeat the Moon Tower wraiths (total: 8)\tMoon Tower wraiths can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should defeat the Moon Tower wraiths and sever their shackles.\n2\tTalk to Dolenthol in Barad Orhant\tDolenthol can be found in Barad Orhant. You should talk to Dolenthol.\n",
[12245]="70038550\n1\tEnter the tavern in upper Woodhurst\tThe nearest inn is near the fountain in the centre of town. You might find Manna and Scurfa at the inn.\n2\tTalk to the innkeeper\tThe innkeeper is behind the bar. The innkeeper may have information about the two former guards you are seeking.\n3\tEnter the tavern in lower Woodhurst\tThe less-frequented inn is in lower Woodhurst. The innkeeper you spoke with suggested looking at a less-frequented -- and likely more dangerous -- inn in town.\n4\tTalk to Manna\tManna and Scurfa, the two former guards, are having drinks at a table in the shady inn in the lower section of Woodhurst. You should speak with Manna and Scurfa.\n5\tTalk to Scurfa\tManna and Scurfa, the two former guards, are having drinks at a table in the shady inn in the lower section of Woodhurst. You should speak with Manna and Scurfa.\n",
[12246]="700544DA\n1\tDefeat the Forsaken Reaver in Mordor Besieged\tFrom the distant south he came, bringing fear and fire to every coast he spied with his glass. His was a reign of blood, and he drew it from all who lived in sight and scent of the Sea. Was that the reason Sauron gave to him the ring Khânto, which is Pain-giver? With the power of it, the Forsaken Reaver could not be stopped, and his laughter carried inland on fell winds; he was among Sauron's swiftest servants, and the cruelest.\n2\tDefeat the Forsaken Reaver in Mordor Besieged\tFrom the distant south he came, bringing fear and fire to every coast he spied with his glass. His was a reign of blood, and he drew it from all who lived in sight and scent of the Sea. Was that the reason Sauron gave to him the ring Khânto, which is Pain-giver? With the power of it, the Forsaken Reaver could not be stopped, and his laughter carried inland on fell winds; he was among Sauron's swiftest servants, and the cruelest.\n3\tThe Forsaken Reaver, defeated but enduring\tFrom the distant south he came, bringing fear and fire to every coast he spied with his glass. His was a reign of blood, and he drew it from all who lived in sight and scent of the Sea. Was that the reason Sauron gave to him the ring Khânto, which is Pain-giver? With the power of it, the Forsaken Reaver could not be stopped, and his laughter carried inland on fell winds; he was among Sauron's swiftest servants, and the cruelest.\n",
[12247]="7004DA64\n1\tAid Spakorth with 'Carving Out A Home'\030Aid Spakorth with 'Forged in Flames'\030Aid Dréri with 'Hunting the North'\030Aid Náth with 'A Costly Journey'\tSpakorth, Náth, and Dréri can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain. Gimli has asked you to aid the Stout-axes in joining with Durin's Folk in Erebor. You should speak to Ambassador Spakorth and his warriors, Náth and Dréri.\n2\tTalk to Ambassador Spakorth\tAmbassador Spakorth can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have aided many of the Stout-axes in settling into their new home, and you should now return to Spakorth.\n",
[12248]="7000178C\n1\tTake the horse from Mincham's Camp to Tham Lorn\tTham Lorn, in the western Fields of Fornost, can be reached by taking the horse from Mincham's Camp. You should travel to Tham Lorn to confront Olnathron once and for all.\n2\tConfront the fell spirit Olnathron\tOlnathron can be found to the west of the graves of his wife and child. Fearing for the strength of his will, Mincham has asked you to find and confront the fell spirit who has taken his wife's semblance.\n3\tReturn to Mincham\tMincham awaits you at his camp. Mincham will be relieved to learn that the fell spirit Olnathron has been sent back to the abyss.\n",
[12249]="70069D1F\n1\tComplete Fortunes of Umbar Baharbêl daily quests (total: 16)\tThe Fortunes of Umbar Baharbêl daily quests are available at the Hunter's Expedition Camp, in Rakhatâb, and in Jax Phanâl.\n2\tCompleted\tCompleted many Fortunes of Umbar Baharbêl daily quests quests, assisting the citizens of Umbar Baharbêl.\n",
[12250]="700267D4\n1\tTalk to the Rohirrim-captain in the Heathfells\tThe Rohirrim-captain is at the encampment in the Heathfells. You should relay the tidings regarding the Dunlendings at Wulf's Cleft to the captain of the Rohirrim outpost.\n",
[12251]="7002819E\n1\tDefeat half-orcs at the White Hand encampment (total: 15)\tThe half-orc servants of the White Hand can be found in the encampment in southern Trum Dreng. You should travel to the encampment and defeat the slavers and murderers who have rallied there.\n2\tReturn to Chief Guto at Lhan Tarren\tGuto now stands in his grandfather's place in Lhan Tarren. You should bring news to Chief Guto that the half-orc trespassers have been driven out of Trum Dreng.\n",
[12252]="70000155\n1\tTalk to Adelard Took\tAdelard Took can be found in the Great Smials in Tuckborough. Brombard Foxtail, the Keeper of the Mathom-house heard rumour of Adelard Took's find and asked you to try and obtain the copy of the Founding Writ from Adelard.\n2\tTalk to Belco Brockhouse\tBelco Brockhouse can be found north of Tuckborough town centre, up the hill and on the right of the path. To his embarassment, Adelard Took revealed that he doesn't have the Founding Writ. A local farmer, Belco Brockhouse, is the one who found the Writ, but he refuses to hand it over to Adelard until someone helps him around his farm.\n",
[12253]="7002B8F9\n1\tThwart Saruman's plans within the Foundry\030Defeat Dhâr in the Smelting Room\030Defeat Gurbák in the Bellows Room\tThwart Saruman's plans within the Foundry by destroying his Ring-forge and defeating his lieutenants.\n",
[12254]="7002BC54\n1\tThwart Saruman's plans within the Foundry\030Defeat Dhâr in the Smelting Room\030Defeat Gurbák in the Bellows Room\tThwart Saruman's plans within the Foundry by destroying his Ring-forge and defeating his lieutenants.\n",
[12255]="70019D30\n1\tPick up a pitcher for Telain Neduil\tPitchers can be found on the terrace near Nembes, and there are three locations to which she would have you bring pitchers of water: parched Elves beneath Telain Neduil, at the base of the ladder that climbs up to the House of Celeborn, and at a gathering of musicians north of Celúrlin. Nembes has asked you to deliver pitchers of cool water to parched Elves.\n2\tPick up a pitcher for the gathering of musicians\tPitchers can be found on the terrace near Nembes, and there are three locations to which she would have you bring pitchers of water: parched Elves beneath Telain Neduil, at the base of the ladder that climbs up to the House of Celeborn, and at a gathering of musicians north of Celúrlin. Nembes has asked you to deliver pitchers of cool water to parched Elves.\n3\tPick up a pitcher for the House of Celeborn\tPitchers can be found on the terrace near Nembes, and there are three locations to which she would have you bring pitchers of water: parched Elves beneath Telain Neduil, at the base of the ladder that climbs up to the House of Celeborn, and at a gathering of musicians north of Celúrlin. Nembes has asked you to deliver pitchers of cool water to parched Elves.\n4\tTalk to Nembes at Celúrlin\tNembes is at Celúrlin, Galadriel's fountain in the centre of Caras Galadhon. You have delivered pitchers of cool water to parched Elves throughout the city and should return now to Nembes.\n",
[12256]="70000078\n1\tFind the missing fourth gear\tThe fourth gear is in a chest at the Dourhand port of Kheledûl, east of Gondamon. Bávor has asked you to recover the fourth missing gear from the Dourhands of Kheledûl.\n2\tBring the fourth gear to Bávor\030Collect Gear\tBávor is in Thorin's Hall, far to the north-west of Kheledûl. Bávor will be pleased to see you have recovered the fourth gear.\n",
})
